                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4664f32f-81b7-4be6-aefb-9a1aa1c83b00",
                        "source_entry_id": "db7edba7-9be9-3db9-9508-b1fc902db71e",
                        "source_sense_id": "64509574-e171-3764-b8ab-1f899e617e2a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Tourismus von sehr vielen Menschen in eine Gegend oder an einen Ort",
                        "target_lang_word": "overtourism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overtourism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                        "entry_id": "89d5b578-4001-3251-aeec-cb67d4efcaa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive tourism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5cc06ac-88bd-4edd-b4c6-eaab9bcbdf38",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "As evidenced in the overtourism concept, residents may become resentful of the intrusions of visitors and visitors' impacts on their ways of living (Figure 9.2). Thus, it is essential that residents are involved and have a strong say […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ca51109-b103-4df6-9f01-2df1076d0922",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "If tourism is a capitalist phenomenon, overtourism is its demented late-capitalist cousin: selfie-stick deaths, all-you-can-eat ships docking at historic ports, stag nights that end in property crimes, the live-streaming of the ruination of fragile natural habitats, et cetera."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d4dcb94-34a3-4c8e-a54d-c10b97200574",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "After years in the making, Venice will on Thursday begin charging day trippers to enter the city in an effort to protect the Unesco world heritage site from the effects of over-tourism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61f4a2cc-85b3-43b9-b577-3587c194e084",
                                                "sense_id": "8493bc8b-2520-31fa-9649-96f5629836d1",
                                                "text": "In Barcelona, the center of recent protests against overtourism in European cities, demonstrators carrying signs reading “Tourists go home” and “Tourism is stealing from us” marched down the city’s so-called Golden Mile, a street flanked by luxury boutiques and high-end hotels, spraying visitors with water outside a Louis Vuitton store."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
